<section class="band band--night">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Inside the workbook</p>
    <h2>A calm space to notice, not fix</h2>
    {#- The pull quote used to be a band of its own, under the eyebrow "The
        value of pause", introducing this section from outside it. It belongs
        inside the thing it introduces. -#}
    <p class="quote-band">&ldquo;You start the healing process when you learn to listen to your
    body.&rdquo;</p>
    <p class="intro-wide">The workbook shows you how to ground yourself in the present moment,
    one simple step at a time. Use the seven steps as a daily or weekly practice whenever you
    need to reset. Getting stuck is fine. Your body resisting is part of the journey. Always
    remember to breathe.</p>
    <div class="cards">
      <div>
        <h3>Guided reflection</h3>
        <p>Every step carries calming imagery to settle you, and gentle prompts to guide you
        inward. No right answers are required and blank is an acceptable answer.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Journal pages</h3>
        <p>Spacious pages for keeping up the listening: what you learned, what your body is
        telling you, and how you found your way back to yourself.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>A daily ritual</h3>
        <p>Use the seven steps as a daily card or a simple ritual. Keep it close and return
        whenever you need to pause and reset.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>The practice, online</h3>
        <p><a href="/book/practice/">The same seven steps on this site</a>, with a breathing
        guide, two short timers and prompts that save privately in your own browser.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="shell band">
  <div class="split split--aside">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">About the author</p>
      <h2>Guiding you gently back to yourself</h2>
      <p>Reem Glasco is a Licensed Professional Counselor Supervisor in Texas who believes
      self-care should not be one more thing to get right. Her approach is spacious and kind:
      meet your nervous system where it is, understand what your body is signalling, and learn
      to pause even in the middle of chaos.</p>
      <p>Effort-less Self-Care distils that philosophy into seven approachable steps, so that
      over time you reset more quickly, settle more deeply, and feel more grounded.</p>
      <p>The same lineage runs through her clinical work:
      <a href="/approach/">NARM, Somatic Experiencing and IFS-informed EMDR</a>, all of which
      begin with sensation rather than analysis. <a href="/about/">More about Reem.</a></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <img class="portrait" src="/assets/img/book-reem.jpg" width="506" height="760" loading="lazy"
       decoding="async" alt="Watercolor of a person resting a hand on their chest, eyes closed, in a moment of calm.">
