<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about the book</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>How much does Effort-less Self-Care cost and where can I buy it?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>$14.95, through <a href="https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/effortless-self-care-reem-glasco/1149690519"
      target="_blank" rel="noopener">Barnes &amp; Noble<span class="vh"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. It is written by Reem Glasco, LPC-S, a Licensed Professional Counselor
      Supervisor in Texas, and the workbook and journal are one volume.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is the journal sold separately from the book?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. It is one book. The workbook sets out the seven steps and the journal pages follow
      them, so you read a step and then write on the pages for it. There is nothing else to buy
      and no second volume to track down.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Can I try the practice without buying anything?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes. <a href="/book/practice/">The full seven-step practice</a> runs on this site for
      free, with a breathing guide, the two short timers and all of the journal prompts. Your
      answers save in your own browser and are never sent anywhere.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>How long does the practice take?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>A few minutes. Two steps have a built-in pause, thirty seconds with a hand on your chest
      and seventeen seconds of sensory grounding, and the rest take as long as you want to give
      them. It is designed to survive a bad morning.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is this a substitute for therapy?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>No. It is a daily noticing practice, not treatment, and it is not a crisis resource. If
      something it surfaces needs more than a journal, that is useful information and a good
      reason to <a href="/contact/">book a consult</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I need to have read it to work with Reem?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Not at all. Clients and supervisees come to the practice without ever having seen it.
      The book exists for the people who want something to do on their own.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
